From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Cygwin: cygwin.din: export GetCommandLine{A,W}@0 from undecorated
 targets

The exports GetCommandLineA@0 and GetCommandLineW@0 named their targets
cygwin_GetCommandLineA@0 and cygwin_GetCommandLineW@0, but the functions
are plain cdecl symbols without that decoration.  ld used to resolve
this through the PE+ stdcall fixup pass; binutils removed that pass for
PE+ (534e9a794c4 "PE+: Remove the stdcall fixup machinery"), after which
the DLL no longer links:

  ld: cannot export cygwin_GetCommandLineA@0: symbol not defined
  ld: cannot export cygwin_GetCommandLineW@0: symbol not defined

Name the real symbols as targets.  The exported names keep their @0, so
the DLL's export table is unchanged, and this links with both old and
new ld.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
--- a/winsup/cygwin/cygwin.din
+++ b/winsup/cygwin/cygwin.din
@@ -665,8 +665,8 @@
 getc_unlocked SIGFE
 getchar SIGFE
 getchar_unlocked SIGFE
-GetCommandLineA@0 = cygwin_GetCommandLineA@0 NOSIGFE
-GetCommandLineW@0 = cygwin_GetCommandLineW@0 NOSIGFE
+GetCommandLineA@0 = cygwin_GetCommandLineA NOSIGFE
+GetCommandLineW@0 = cygwin_GetCommandLineW NOSIGFE
 getcontext NOSIGFE
 getcwd SIGFE
 getdelim = __getdelim SIGFE
-- 
2.54.0
